📘 System Maintenance Tools – Quick Summary

1. Hardware Tools

  - Tool	Purpose
  - Screwdrivers (Phillips & Flathead)	Open computer cases
  - Anti-static wrist strap	Prevent ESD damage
  - Compressed air	Remove dust from components
  - Thermal paste & applicator	Improve heat transfer (CPU/cooler)
  - Multimeter	Check connectivity/continuity

2. Network Tools

  - Tool	Purpose
  - Crimper	Attach connectors to cables
  - Cable stripper	Remove cable insulation
  - Toner probe	Trace cables through walls
  - Punchdown tool	Wire connections at the rack
  - Loopback plug	Test interface connectivity

3. Software Tools

  - Tool	Purpose
  - Task Manager	Monitor system performance
  - Disk Clean-up	Free up disk space
  - Check Disk (chkdsk)	Check hard drive health
  - MemTest86	Test RAM for errors
  - BIOS/UEFI utilities	Configure hardware settings
  - Note: Task Manager, Disk Clean-up, and chkdsk are Windows utilities.

4. Preventative Maintenance Best Practices

  - Regular dust cleaning – especially fans and vents
  - Keep drivers and firmware up-to-date
  - Check system logs for errors
  - Backup data regularly – and test recovery!
  - Monitor system performance
